## 2. Non-Negotiable Safety & Git Invariants

### Git Guardrails — STRICTLY FORBIDDEN Without Human Confirmation
1. **Never push commits to any remote repository** without explicit, per-action human confirmation.
2. **Never create Pull Requests** or merge branches autonomously.
3. Keep all git operations strictly local (`git add`, `git diff`, `git status`, local commits).

### Secret & Credential Safety
1. **Never commit secrets, tokens, API keys, or credentials.**
2. Never store `.env` files in source control.
3. Obey all enterprise secret scanner findings.

{{domain_invariants}}

