## 3. Working With Cadence Goals (`scripts/cadence.py`)

When helping the developer plan or execute work:
- Check current active goals: `python3 scripts/cadence.py list --scope daily --status active`
- Advance goal phase: `python3 scripts/cadence.py advance <goal_id> --phase <phase>`
- Mark complete: `python3 scripts/cadence.py complete <goal_id>`
- Weekly planning: `python3 scripts/cadence.py week-plan`

---

## 4. Working With the Knowledge Base (`wiki/`)

- All wiki pages in `wiki/` have YAML frontmatter with `title`, `date`, `category`, `tags`, `sources`.
- Never modify files in `docs/` or `raw/` if present (those are human-authored sources).
- When creating or editing wiki pages, re-synchronize the database index:
  ```bash
  python3 scripts/export_wiki.py && python3 scripts/sync_wiki_db.py
  ```

---

## 5. Drift Enforcement & Stamping Discipline

- The project tracks file and symbol integrity via `docs/drift_registries/*.json`.
- **NEVER stamp registries autonomously.** Stamping requires explicit human approval during session wrapup.
- To check for drift: `python3 scripts/drift_enforcer.py`.

---

## 6. Implementation Plan Preservation

- When formulating complex plans, write design proposals under `docs/decisions/`.
- Use unique versioned names: `YYYY-MM-DD-feature-name-implementation-plan.md`.
- Never overwrite existing decision records.
